  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FOC Capacity Building</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is about FOC Director to attend Human Rights Advocacy training at Columbia University in New York. The training is organized by the Centre for the Study of Human Rights.   The study focuses on Human Rights and Globalization, and provides extensive training and technical assistance to leaders from NGOs working to secure rights for those who have traditionally been excluded from decision making processes on the global level. It emphasizes on building the capacity of local actors and their organizations. It seeks to provide advance training on advocacy knowledge on how to use international human rights mechanisms to seek redress for rights violations, and connection to the policy makers, NGOs etc. As a capacity building support project, the knowledge and skills acquired will enhance the finalization of FOC&#x2019;s strategic planning process which is advocacy work focused.</narrative>
  </description>
